{"authored" [{"question" "q-147668" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(1,0)$, $(0,-3)$ and $(-2,1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n\n- $(12,-24)$\n- $(8,16)$\n- $(2,-4)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/state.json" "file_sha256" "14476014320fedf4d1a6acd7b6131a6a9a2aeec40dc6c5bc972ee7ec8ac4d420" "basis" 1050 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-147668" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 12 & -8 \\\\ -4 & -24 & 16\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(2,-4)$, $(12,-24)$ and $(-8,16).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/state.json" "file_sha256" "14476014320fedf4d1a6acd7b6131a6a9a2aeec40dc6c5bc972ee7ec8ac4d420" "basis" 1050 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-147668" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3117cac283fb94cc19d5fe97a6acc1c3e0354b103cbb0237db3b15f187694112" "basis" 1050 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-147668" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/state.json" "file_sha256" "14476014320fedf4d1a6acd7b6131a6a9a2aeec40dc6c5bc972ee7ec8ac4d420" "basis" 1050 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-147668" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/state.json" "file_sha256" "14476014320fedf4d1a6acd7b6131a6a9a2aeec40dc6c5bc972ee7ec8ac4d420" "basis" 1050 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-147668" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/state.json" "file_sha256" "14476014320fedf4d1a6acd7b6131a6a9a2aeec40dc6c5bc972ee7ec8ac4d420" "basis" 1050 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-147668" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/1399313